WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.502
-Ray Donovan
is a fixer of sorts on the show.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you talk to people
who had those --

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
that type of profession
before you started doing this?

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.275
-No, I talked to lawyers.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
I talked to --

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
´Cause lawyers are actually
the Ray Donovans of --

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, not entirely.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
But lawyers,
I talked to security guys,

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.986
bodyguards, private detectives.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.955
It´s just that Ray sort of does
a little bit of everything.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.356
And there have been guys,

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
particularly in the Golden Age
of movies, who did it all.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:29.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But none of those guys
are around anymore.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think it --
You know, I really think

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.501
it was a brilliant move
by Ann to kind of predict

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
that our culture
would become so spin-obsessed.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That a character
like Ray Donovan would --

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
would really
be a compelling character.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it feels
like everyone these days --

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.645
You would not be surprised
to know if anyone in politics

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:46.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
had a fixer.
-That´s right.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.847
-You would say, "Of course.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would be silly
<i>not </i>to have a fixer.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s sort of de rigueur now.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.086
-When you talk to those guys,

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
people that were
in the bodyguard business,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.756 size:88% position:44%
the security business,
are they excited to talk

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
to an actor
who´s about play that type?

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:02.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think people
are always generally excited

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:05.331
to talk to an actor who´s about
to play them, I think.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess they have a chance,
too, to try to, like,

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.435 size:78% position:39%
politic and make sure
you do it in a way

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.769
that makes them seem cooler.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.405
-I think Marty Baron was
probably the exception to that.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right.
Sure, of course.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.809 size:75% position:38%
-I took a train down
to meet Marty Baron,

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I am a huge fan of
as an editor.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.347 size:84% position:42%
A great admirer of his.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.417
And I don´t think there could´ve
been two more nervous guys

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a room than me
and Marty Baron talking to --

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.890
He´s not someone
who I think really is interested

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
in his own story.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yeah, I would imagine
because he´s so much

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the side of the news
that presents it.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Like, I -- It strikes me

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
as he´s someone who believes
the more invisible he is

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.699
the better the news story.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The better he is
at doing his job, yeah.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.635
-He must´ve been psyched,
though, that Liev Schreiber

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
was playing him, right?
-I don´t know.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-If I´m Marty Baron

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I see Ray Donovan walk in,
I´m a little worried.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.175
-Yeah, I think so, too, yeah.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, Ray Donovan
comes from Boston.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He does.
-He´s from Southie.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.782
So you have to, as an actor --

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.884
One of the great hurdles of any
actor is the Boston accent.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-How do you feel?

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.086
Do you feel good about it?

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.055
-I feel like we did okay.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
I fee like I´m pretty good
at it --

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.225 size:81% position:41%
-That´s the best grade

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
you´ll ever get
from a person from Boston.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What´s that?
-"Okay."

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.430
Yeah, no one from Boston
is like, "You did it, bro.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
We´re so proud of you."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:12.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It´s all right."

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"We´re so proud a kid
from New York got it right."

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-"No, you did good."

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went to school
in Massachusetts,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I used to hang out
with a guy

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was a crazy Pats fan
from Southie.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.810
And I kind of -- I´m kind of
ripping him off a little bit.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we did make
one huge mistake...

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...that any Southie
probably knows,

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
if there are any Southies
in the house tonight.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
We called the character
Ray Donovan.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah,
that´s what I would´ve done.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s "Dunovan."
-"Dunovan." Interesting.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:41.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you´re a Southie or Irish,
it´s "Dunovan," and, uh...

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we´ve been screwing it up
for six years, but, uh...

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.064 size:84% position:42%
-But I´m sure people --

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.400
-We´ve got another season
of "Ray Donovan" coming.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Well, you should --

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.504
There should be a moment where,
like, you get a --

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, maybe you do
one of those shows,

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
like Ray Donovan --
Here´s just a pitch.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.243
-You do, like, one of those
"finding your roots" shows.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like, the character.
-Oh, it goes back?

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He goes back
and finds hit root.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.915 size:81% position:41%
And then the character
finds out, they say,

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:04.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Actually, it´s Dunovan,"
and then you just change it.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s brilliant.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s brilliant.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s brilliant.
-I´m gonna tell David.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, okay, perfect.
Thanks so much for being here.

